  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the insurance law, in relation to requiring certain large\ngroup health insurance policies and contracts to cover scalp cooling systems\nfor the preservation of hair during cancer chemotherapy treatment; to amend a\nchapter of the laws of 2024 amending the insurance law relating to providing\nhealth insurance coverage for scalp cooling systems for the preservation of\nhair during cancer chemotherapy treatment, as proposed in legislative bills\nnumbers S. 2063-A and A. 38-A, in relation to the effectiveness thereof; and\nto repeal certain provisions of the insurance law relating thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S774",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S774-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Rpld §3216 sub§ (i) ¶12-b, amd §§3221 & 4303, Ins L; amd §4, Chap of 2024 (as proposed in S.2063-A & A.38-A)",
    "lawSection": "Insurance Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S774\n\nSPONSOR: STAVISKY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the insurance law, in relation to requiring certain\nlarge group health insurance policies and contracts to cover scalp cool-\ning systems for the preservation of hair during cancer chemotherapy\ntreatment; to amend a chapter of the laws of 2024 amending the insurance\nlaw relating to providing health insurance coverage for scalp cooling\nsystems for the preservation of hair during cancer chemotherapy treat-\nment, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 2063-A and A. 38-A, in\nrelation to the effectiveness thereof; and to repeal certain provisions\nof the insurance law relating thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2024\nC.595 related to coverage for scalp cooling systems used to preserve\nhair during cancer chemotherapy treatment.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter to apply to large group\ninsurance policies.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 595 of the laws of 2024. S.2063-A and\nA.38-A passed in their respective houses in June 2024.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2024 amending the insurance law relating to\nproviding health insurance coverage for scalp cooling systems for the\npreservation of hair during cancer chemotherapy treatment, as proposed\nin legislative bills numbers S. 2063-A and A. 38-A, takes effect.\n",
